COPY wced.example (exampleid, senseid, text_cebuano, text_translation) FROM stdin;
1	10004	Kanang isdáa, dílì kadtu,	That fish there, not that one further over.
2	10004	Háing baláya ang íla?	Which house is theirs?
3	10005	Dakù ang amúang balay, gamay tung iláha,	Our house is large, and theirs is small.
4	10006	Dakúa uy!	My! How big it is!
5	10006	Patyun tikaw, irúa ka!	I’ll kill you, you dog you!
6	10006	Ngilngígang awtúha à!	That’s some car!
7	10008	Á, muanhi ka ugmà?	Um, are you going to come here tomorrow?
8	10009	Á, paríha ra nákù,	Oh, it’s all the same to me.
9	10009	Á, nagkumidiya lang siya,	Oh, he’s just joking.
10	10010	Á, dì nà mahímù,	Oh, you can’t do that.
11	10011	Á, duha diay tu,	Oh, yes. There were two of them, weren’t there.
12	10012	Á, Lítu diay ímung ngálan,	Oh, so your name is Lito.
13	10012	Á, kanindut,	Oh, how nice!
14	10013	Á, nahuwasan ku,	Ah, what a relief!
15	10015	À, mu ra diay nà? Kasayun à!	Oh, is that all there is to it? How easy it is!
16	10015	À, ása man ku mutúu nímu,	Hm, you think I could believe you?
17	10016	À, hináya nímung mulíhuk,	Hm! You sure work slowly!
18	10017	À, kanindut nímug sinínà,	How come you have such a beautiful dress on!
19	10020	Aba! Nakadaug ku,	My! I won!
20	10021	Ábà tuy, maáyu ka lang sa tayáda, wà kay tadtad,	Shut up! You’re great at talking, but let’s see you do s.t.
21	10022	Abaa! Mahū́g ka gánì dihà!	Stop that! You might fall!
22	10024	Gipakatagaabab lang ku ninyu. Ihása,	You just think I’m a hillbilly. Don’t try to fool me.
23	10027	Ab-ábun sa irù ang íyang hikut,	The dog will chew up his rope.
24	10028	Ang pagluib ni Maríya nag-ab-ab sa íyang balatían,	Maria’s infidelity ate away at his insides.
25	10028	Giab-ab ang íyang pinútì sa tayà,	His sword was eaten away by rust.
26	10029	Ang nag-ab-ab kung núka,	My festering wound.†
27	10031	Kinsa may mag-ábag nímu sa ímung pag-iskuyla?	Who will help pay for your schooling?
28	10031	Abági ku áring pagsilhig,	Help me sweep.
29	10037	Abagáhun (pangabagáhun, pangabagáhan) ni Mánuy níya ang galastúhan sa pag-iskuyla,	His brother will shoulder his school expenses.
30	10038	Kita giyuy muabága (mangabága) áning prugramáha,	We must undertake to carry out this program.
31	10042	Abáhu (báhu) 	I am bound by my husband’s decisions.
32	10052	Ug ikaw muabalu sa ákung yútà, ayawg dak-a,	If you assess my land, don’t set it too high.
33	10052	Ang yútà miabalu (giabalu, giabaluhan) ug singkwinta mil,	The land was assessed at fifty thousand pesos.
34	10053	Purus dagkug abalwasiyun ang mga yútà dinhi sa syudad,	The lots in the city all have high assessments.
35	10054	Nag-abandunar na lang siya sa íyang kaugalíngun sukad mamatay ang íyang asáwa,	He neglected himself entirely after his wife died.
36	10054	Ayaw abandunaha (iabandunar) ang ímung pamilya,	Do not abandon your family.
37	10059	Ang usa ka kwartu giabángan sa tigúlang,	The old man rents one of the rooms.
38	10061	Iábang ni nákung baktína álang sa uma,	I will sacrifice this pig as rental for the land.
39	10062	Pilay ábang nímu sa libru?	How much rent did you pay for the book?
40	10064	Kadtung nalumus dinhi ábang kunu tu sa ingkantu,	The man who drowned here is said to have been the rent collected by the supernatural spirit.
41	10067	Abangan kunu kanang baláya. Náa giyuy mamatay káda túig,	That house is haunted (lit. has a rental on it). Each year s.o. dies there.
42	10069	Iabánid (abaníra) kini pagpintal arun dílì magkampat,	Paint it one square at a time so it will come out even.
43	10070	Abánid ang íyang pagsukut sa mga istudyanti,	He asked the students one after another in turn.
44	10081	Naabansáda sa hángin ang ákung bukubuku, maung gisip-un ku,	My back was directly exposed to the wind. That’s why I caught cold.
45	10081	Ayaw abansadáha (iabansáda) sa hángin ang inyung bintánà,	Don’t put a window right where it catches the full breeze.
46	10083	Ang mga Hapúnis miabansin sa pátag sa Lusun,	The Japanese advanced over the plains of Luzon.
47	10084	Abanti ka rang milingkud,	You took a seat too far to the front.
48	10086	Muabanti kag diyútay, matambug ka sa bangag,	If you move forward any more, you will fall into the hole.
49	10086	Iabanti nang ímung awtug diyútay,	Move your car forward a bit.
50	10087	Naabantíhan mu námug diyis puntus,	We were ten points ahead of you.
51	10088	Dì ku makaabanti sa galastúhan sa iskuylahan,	I cannot keep up with the school payments.
52	10089	Dì ku makaabanti sa pagdáru kay dautun ku,	I can’t keep up with the plowing because I’m sickly.
53	10092	Nahiyus ang abanti sa mutur,	The front tire of the motorcycle is flat.
54	10102	Maapsan pa nímu siya ug ímung abatun sa iskína,	You can still catch up with him if you head him off at the corner.
55	10103	Ig-ági níya, abta siya,	When he comes by, give him a scare.
56	10109	Wà giyud mi magkítà, nag-abat-ábat lang,	We just kept missing each other.
57	10110	Ang tigúwang miábat sa pasamánu paingun sa táas,	The old man held on to the bannister while going upstairs.
58	10112	Nag-ábat siya sa yáwi sa íyang bulsa kung wà ba hibyai,	He felt for the key in his pocket to see if he hadn’t left it behind.
59	10112	Abátun ku ang íyang agtang ug hilanatun ba,	I’ll touch her forehead to see if she is feverish.
60	10113	Nakaabat ku sa kabugnaw sa sinihan,	I felt the coolness of the movie house.
61	10113	Abátun gánì nímu ang kasakit, musamut giyud,	If you think about the pain, it will get worse.
62	10114	Nakaabat kung mu rag may misaka sa ámung báy,	I sensed that s.o. had entered our house.
63	10115	Lagmit hiligsan ang bátà kay nag-abay sa tartanilya,	The child is likely to be run over because he is running alongside of the rig.
64	10115	Silang duha nag-ábay paglanguy,	The two swam side by side.
65	10116	Pagkatáwu sa ákung iyaan, giabayan (giabyan) ug sawa. Mau nang nadátù ang íyang inahan,	When my aunt was born, a twin snake was born with her, and so her mother became rich.
66	10117	Ug mupalit kag usa ka sákung humay muabay kug lima ka gantang,	If you buy a sack of rice, I will go in with you for five ganta’s worth.
67	10117	Giabyan níyag singku písus ang ákung pusta,	He went in for five pesos on my bet.
68	10120	Ang ákung abay bálig dus písus ra,	My share is two pesos’ worth.
69	10123	Ása man ning dyípa, bay?	Where is this jeep headed for, driver?
70	10127	Alang kaníya walà siyay láing abyan kun dílì álak,	He has no other friend except liquor.
71	10130	Kita lay mag-abyan,	Let’s be friends.
72	10131	Walà siya makig-abyan sa huguyhúguy,	He did not indulge in roaming about.
